16. AP credit compared with transferred courses
Question: Can AP credit satisfy the writing or quantitative reasoning requirements, and how does that differ from transferring a college course?
Expected answer: AP credit cannot satisfy these requirements. Eligible transferred college courses may satisfy quantitative reasoning and one writing requirement, but not the remaining two writing requirements or intercultural literacy.
Source document ID(s): registrar-transfer-credits; registrar-graduation-requirements provides corroborating requirements.
Expected evidence: “AP credits may not be used to fulfill any of the Domain or Skills requirements.” “Students may transfer courses to fulfill the ‘Q’ and one ‘W’ requirement but not the ‘C’ or final two ‘W’ requirements.”
Answerable: Yes. This can be answered from registrar-transfer-credits alone.

17. Taking a quantitative reasoning course elsewhere
Question: I want to take a course at another college to meet Beloit’s quantitative reasoning requirement. What should I do before enrolling, and what minimum grade would make it eligible for transfer?
Expected answer: Complete the Transfer Credit Authorization Form before enrolling and have the proposed credit reviewed. A transferred course may fulfill Q, and a grade of C or better is required for transfer eligibility. Approval is not automatic.
Source document ID(s): registrar-transfer-credits
Expected evidence: “Students enrolled at Beloit who wish to transfer credits for coursework taken after matriculation should complete the Transfer Credit Authorization Form prior to enrolling in a course elsewhere.” “The quantitative reasoning requirement may be fulfilled with a transfer course.” “A grade of ‘C’ or better is required for the credit to transfer.”
Answerable: Yes.

18. Withdrawing with a WP
Question: I missed the normal drop deadline but am still earning a D. Can I request a WP, what documentation is needed, and will I receive credit?
Expected answer: You may petition for a WP; approval is not guaranteed. Provide your written petition, an instructor statement confirming a D or better, and an advisor statement. Submit by the semester’s last day of classes. The Academic Performance Committee approves the withdrawal. A WP appears on the transcript but earns no credit.
Source document ID(s): registrar-registration; catalog-grading-policy also describes WP approval.
Expected evidence: “Have the instructor provide a written statement verifying that the student was passing the course with a ‘D’ or better grade at the time of the request.” “Have their advisor provide a written statement.” “No credit is granted for a course in which a WP is received, but the course appears on the transcript with a grade of ‘WP’.” “A petition to the Academic Performance Committee to withdraw from a course with a ‘WP’ grade must be submitted no later than the last day of classes of the semester in which the course is being taken.”
Answerable: Yes.

